    feat: --gdb mode for fast (QEMU stub) and cycle (vsim JTAG + ICEman)

    - `--gdb` on fast: injects `-gdb tcp::1234 -S` into the QEMU standalone
      invocation (pauses at reset, waits for GDB on port 1234)
    - `--gdb` on cycle: forks vsim with `--jtag-port 9104`, then execs ICEman
      (`$ICEMAN` env var) with `-Z v5` in the foreground
    - `--gdb-port PORT` overrides the default port for either model
    - `--gdb` rejected on hybrid with a clear error
    - `--gdb-port` validated to require `--gdb` (consistent with cosim-interval pattern)
    - Fix: resolve ELF to absolute path in run_standalone; QEMU -bios searches
      its data directory for relative paths instead of the CWD
    - Refactor: abs_elf() helper dedups ELF absolutization across run_standalone
      and run_cycle_gdb; spawn_inherit() gains a wait=false path so fork_background
      is a one-liner instead of duplicating the child exec block
    - docs: add GDB section to andes_sim_demo.ipynb with a runnable batch session

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

